// The ORIGINAL policy of passing case 1121 (now
// `1121_pin_not_bypassed_by_fresh_binder`): an attempt to bypass the event
// schema's principal pin by binding the pinned field to a FREE variable
// (`callerPrincipal: p`) used nowhere else, so the author's own constraint
// is vacuous — "a Login by anyone".
//
// Post-closedness, this shape never reaches pin injection at all: a temporal
// leaf with a free variable is rejected at parse time, schema-independently
// (so the harness's unpinned fixture event schema is irrelevant — the
// rejection precedes event-schema derivation). The bypass attempt that
// remains *expressible* is the exists-bound variant, which the passing case
// keeps under test: the fresh binder still binds-but-never-constrains, and
// the injected pin still forces the past Login to share the current
// request's principal.
//
// Expected: rejected at parse-time binding checks — temporal leaves must be
// closed.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user, callerPrincipal: p }
};
